//Problem: Scholarship Selection
A college is selecting students for a scholarship based on three subject marks.
A student qualifies only if:
- Their total marks are at least 200.
- Their marks in each subject are at least 50.
You are given the marks of three subjects: A, B, and C.
Determine whether the student qualifies.
Input Format
- First line contains T, the number of test cases.
- Each test case contains three integers A, B, and C.
Output Format
Print:
- YES if the student qualifies.
- NO otherwise.


solution:-
#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
    int t,a,b,c,total;
    scanf("%d",&t);
    while(t--){
        scanf("%d %d %d",&a,&b,&c);
        total=a+b+c;
        if(a>=50 && b>=50 && c>=50){
            if(total>=200)
                printf("YES\n");
            else
                printf("NO\n");
        } else {
            printf("No\n");
        }
    }
}
